invariant: INV-28
file: srv_flight.c
catches: srv_rec_test
reason: the compatibility change_cipher_spec, the one record a server sends
  when the client's hello carries a legacy_session_id, goes out through
  cfg.send instead of the driver's own output. A TRANSPORT=record server
  then writes to a socket it promised never to touch, and a caller whose
  send refuses during the handshake fails every handshake with a
  middlebox-compatibility client such as Go's crypto/tls, which is how
  colibri found it. test/srv_rec_test.c sends a hello with a 32-byte
  session id and requires the record from on_record_out.

--- old
    return srv_out_record(h->t, rec, n);
--- new
    return h->t->cfg.send(h->t->cfg.io, rec, n) == 0 ? CH_OK : CH_EIO;
